feat: --print-qemu-config -- bake the engine's QEMU -readconfig cfg

Each engine now carries a QEMU -readconfig cfg distilled from its
config.inc, so a hybrid run's QEMU fast-forward leg executes the same ISA
the cycle-accurate engine models (CoDense, Zfh, Zb*, xandesv5isa, ...).

- Bake (cmake/VerilatorHelpers.cmake): run config_inc_to_qemu_cfg.py
  --cpu-model <family> on the engine's config.inc -> obj_sc/qemu.cfg ->
  ld -r -b binary -> qemu_cfg.o -> archived into V<RTL>__ALL.a, exactly
  like config.inc. The generator is the new cpu_config_to_march_converter
  submodule (external/); its path is the CPU_CONFIG_QEMU_CONVERTER cache
  var (set empty to disable, embedding an empty cfg).
- CLI (src/main.cpp): --print-qemu-config dumps the embedded blob,
  mirroring --print-config. Empty when no converter is configured.

The andesim driver consumes this via -readconfig (its
docs/qemu_match_ROADMAP.md).

Behavioral change.

